# EOL policy: the repository stores LF for all text files; working-tree conversion is
# left to core.autocrlf (Windows) or none (CI). Normalizing on `git add` keeps ZIP-imported
# or externally edited files (mixed CRLF/LF) from ever committing CRLF blobs.
* text=auto

# Explicit text types
*.kt text
*.java text
*.xml text
*.kts text
*.json text
*.md text
*.toml text
*.properties text
*.pro text
*.gradle text

# Scripts: keep CRLF where cmd.exe needs it, LF where shells need it (checkout-time only;
# both normalize to LF in the index).
*.bat text
gradlew text

# Binary assets: never normalize
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
